1. Review, in parallel. Run `git diff a1b2c3d4e5f6a7b8c9d0e1f2a3b4c5d6e7f8a9b0..HEAD` once. Then, in a single message, start four subagents with the Agent tool, each read-only (no edits, no commits), each given that diff and exactly one angle below. Each goes file by file through every hunk, tests and styles included, and returns every finding, small ones too (a wrapper or helper with one caller, an expression, call or literal repeated in the change, a duplicated declaration or test fixture, a value computed twice), unranked and unfiltered, each with the file, the line, a one-line summary, the concrete cost (what is duplicated, wasted or harder to maintain) and the fix it would make:
